 "integration": {
  "summary": "Register the BACnet connection license, set the LAN2 (BACnet) IP and the device number with the BACnet Setting Tool, and wait for the controller to go ONLINE. Then map the per-group objects (01GGPP): On Off, mode, setpoint, room temp and alarm. Write only when a setting changes, never cyclically.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BO 10101",
    "name": "On Off Setup",
    "why": "Start/stop the group"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 10102",
    "name": "On Off State",
    "why": "Confirm run status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MO 10105",
    "name": "Operational Mode Setup",
    "why": "Command the operating mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MI 10106",
    "name": "Operational Mode State",
    "why": "Read back the active mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10110",
    "name": "Set Temp",
    "why": "Setpoint for single-setpoint groups"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10124",
    "name": "Set Temp Cool",
    "why": "Cooling setpoint, dual-setpoint groups"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10125",
    "name": "Set Temp Heat",
    "why": "Heating setpoint, dual-setpoint groups"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 10109",
    "name": "Room Temp",
    "why": "Space temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 10103",
    "name": "Alarm Signal",
    "why": "Group fault alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 10120",
    "name": "M-NET Communication State",
    "why": "M-NET link to the group lost"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BACnet only runs when the controller is in ONLINE mode, which needs a valid BACnet connection license and consistent BACnet settings. Changing group/interlock settings sends it back to OFFLINE; returning to ONLINE can take up to about 10 minutes on large systems. Local remote-controller lockouts are the Prohibition BVs (13-17) per group.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet uses the LAN2 port (100BASE-TX); LAN1 and LAN2 must be on different networks and on separate switches. LAN2 cannot be used for cloud connection when BACnet is on.",
   "UDP 47808 recommended for unicast and broadcast; Class C private address recommended (192.168.2.1 to 192.168.254.254).",
   "Protocol revision is selectable in the BACnet Setting Tool (Rev.12 or Rev.21); pick Rev.12 for BMS front ends at Rev.4-11.",
   "Device number, COV and event notification destinations and which objects are used are set in the BACnet Setting Tool; the manual gives no default device instance.",
   "Each AE-C/EW-C is configured separately; the Setting Tool handles one controller at a time."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "WriteProperty limit: 24 writes per day per property, 200 ms between writes. Do not rewrite on/off, setpoint, mode or prohibitions periodically; the units keep settings in nonvolatile memory.",
   "Read interval: 200 ms per property; after a ReadPropertyMultiple of N properties wait N x 200 ms.",
   "M-NET communication errors with a unit set Alarm Signal, Error Code, Error Code Detail and M-NET Communication State; the alarm part depends on the 'Not reflect communication error to alarm signal' setting.",
   "If System Forced Off cannot be cleared from the BMS (for example after a comms fault), it can be force-reset from the BACnet Setting Tool.",
   "Some property values are saved to nonvolatile memory only every 30 or 60 minutes, so a power cut can roll them back.",
   "Energy accumulators and their trend logs need the Charge license."
  ]
 },
 "page": "https://easybacnet.com/bacnet-points-lists/mitsubishi-electric/ae-c400-ew-c50",
 "note": "Re-typed from the manufacturer's public documentation (see source). Point availability varies by firmware and options; verify against the live device."
